OR=[0,[15,0],dd],kO5=UT,kO6=CY,kO7=ahT,kO8=Ly,kO1=UT,kO2=CY,kO3=ahT,kO4=Ly,kOX=[0,UT],kOY=[0,CY],kOZ=[0,ahT],kO0=[0,Ly],kOT=UT,kOU=CY,kOV=ahT,kOW=Ly,kOS=dHh,kPo=[0,d0W],kPp=[0,d0W],kPq=[0,"selection_anchor_point_origin"],kPm=m,kPn=m,kPl="Caret.point: Inner caret with empty selection",kPk=[0,"caret_point_charsel"],kPh=[0,c$D],kPi=[0,c$D],kPj=[0,0,0],kPe=m,kPf=m,kPd=[0,0,0],kPc=[0,dtV,58,2],kPb=[0,dtV,49,2],kPa=[0,0],kPr='\nCreates a task plan with a title, description, and subtask milestones.\nSets this as the active task. The first subtask becomes active automatically.\n\nDoes NOT modify the Hazel program, probes, statics, or syntax projectors \xe2\x80\x94 only the workbench.\nYou must still call edit tools (update_*, insert_*, delete_*) and placement tools (place_probe, place_statics, place_syntax_projector, \xe2\x80\xa6) to change what the user sees.\n\nOptional: use this for **larger or multi-turn** efforts where a visible plan helps (features, big refactors, many steps). **Skip** for trivial or one-shot edits \xe2\x80\x94 small fixes do not need a task; edits are not required to be tied to any task.\n\nWhen you do use it: subtasks should be meaningful milestones (e.g., "Implement core logic", "Add tests"),\nnot individual tool calls (e.g., NOT "update definition", "add line break").\nAim for 1-4 subtasks per task. Each subtask represents a logical stage of work.\n\nParameters:\ntask: {\n  title: string \xe2\x80\x94 concise name (serves as unique identifier)\n  description: string \xe2\x80\x94 detailed explanation of the goal, approach, and relevant context\n  subtasks: list({\n    title: string \xe2\x80\x94 concise milestone name (serves as unique identifier)\n    description: string \xe2\x80\x94 what this milestone involves and any implementation notes\n  })\n}\n',kPs=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,[0,[0,awZ,[0,Q,[0,okG,okF]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,[0,[0,g,awZ],0]]],0]]]]],0],kPt=dT,kPu=[0,ck,[0,g,a$c]],kPv=eN,kPw=[0,b8,[0,g,eN]],kPx="\nDescription:\nUnsets the currently active task in the composition model.\nThis results in no active task being set.\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nExample(s):\nCalling unset_active_task() will result in no active task being set in the composition model.\n",kPy=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,0]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,0]],0]]]]],0],kPz=dT,kPA=[0,ck,[0,g,bhh]],kPB=eN,kPC=[0,b8,[0,g,eN]],kPD='\nDescription:\nSets the active task in the composition model to the task with the given title.\n\nParameters:\ntitle: string \xe2\x80\x94 the title of the task to set as active\n\nExample(s):\nCalling set_active_task(title = "Task 1") will set the active task in the composition model to the task with the title "Task 1".\nThe title must match the title of an existing task in the task dictionary.\n',kPE=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,[0,[0,fb,[0,Q,[0,okI,okH]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,[0,[0,g,fb],0]]],0]]]]],0],kPF=dT,kPG=[0,ck,[0,g,a$T]],kPH=eN,kPI=[0,b8,[0,g,eN]],kPJ="\nDescription:\nUnsets the currently active subtask in the active task.\nThis results in no active subtask being set for the currently active task.\nThis requires an active task to be set, otherwise nothing will happen.\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nExample(s):\nCalling unset_active_subtask() will result in no active subtask being set for the currently active task.\n",kPK=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,0]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,0]],0]]]]],0],kPL=dT,kPM=[0,ck,[0,g,bj_]],kPN=eN,kPO=[0,b8,[0,g,eN]],kPP='\nDescription:\nSets the active subtask in the active task to the subtask with the given title.\n\nParameters:\ntitle: string \xe2\x80\x94 the title of the subtask to set as active\n\nExample(s):\nCalling set_active_subtask(title = "Subtask 1") will set the active subtask in the active task to the subtask with the title "Subtask 1".\nThe title must match the title of an existing subtask in the subtasks of the active task.\n',kPQ=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,[0,[0,fb,[0,Q,[0,okK,okJ]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,[0,[0,g,fb],0]]],0]]]]],0],kPR=dT,kPS=[0,ck,[0,g,bmz]],kPT=eN,kPU=[0,b8,[0,g,eN]],kPV="\nMarks the active task as complete with a summary describing what was accomplished.\nThis tool only updates the workbench \xe2\x80\x94 it does NOT edit code or place probes/statics/projectors.\nOnly use it after the corresponding program and overlay changes were already applied via the appropriate tools.\n\nThe summary is visible to the user \xe2\x80\x94 make it clear and informative.\nAny subtasks that are still open are **automatically marked complete** with a short system note when you call this tool, so you do not need to call `mark_active_subtask_complete` on each one first.\n\nParameters:\nsummary: string \xe2\x80\x94 a clear description of what was built/changed and how it works (must match edits/placements you actually ran)\n",kPW=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,[0,[0,ET,[0,Q,[0,okM,okL]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,[0,[0,g,ET],0]]],0]]]]],0],kPX=dT,kPY=[0,ck,[0,g,biE]],kPZ=eN,kP0=[0,b8,[0,g,eN]],kP1="\nDescription:\nMarks the active task as incomplete.\nThis requires an active task to be set, otherwise nothing will happen.\n\nParameters:\nNone\n",kP2=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,0]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,0]],0]]]]],0],kP3=dT,kP4=[0,ck,[0,g,bmO]],kP5=eN,kP6=[0,b8,[0,g,eN]],kP7="\nMarks the active subtask as complete and automatically advances to the next incomplete subtask.\nDoes NOT modify the program or overlays \xe2\x80\x94 only the workbench. Call edit and placement tools first.\n\nIf all subtasks are complete, no subtask will be active; you can then call `mark_active_task_complete` (which also auto-completes any remaining open subtasks if you skip straight to it).\n\nParameters:\nsummary: string \xe2\x80\x94 a brief description of what was done to complete this milestone (must reflect real tool-driven changes)\n",kP8=[0,[0,k8,[0,Q,[0,[0,b8,[0,g,jv]],[0,[0,kg,[0,Q,[0,[0,ET,[0,Q,[0,okO,okN]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,h,[0,[0,g,ET],0]]],0]]]]],0],kP9=dT,kP_